{
  "formId": "ARD04.QF.003",
  "formTitle": "Emigration Clearance Certificate (ECC) Application Form",
  "documentType": "application_request",
  "availability": "active",
  "checkoutEligible": null,
  "checkoutEligibleNote": "Not yet decided -- same open business-classification question as the other mapped forms. This mapping covers field-level automation only; checkout eligibility is a separate business decision.",
  "reproductionRightsVerified": true,
  "reproductionRightsNote": "Confirmed directly on the form itself: 'THIS DOCUMENT MAY BE REPRODUCED AND IS NOT FOR SALE', printed at the top of the page.",
  "pageWidthPt": 612,
  "pageHeightPt": 971.04,
  "sourcePdf": "original.pdf",
  "derivedFrom": "Measured from a 300 DPI raster of the real original PDF (downloaded from the private fis-bi-forms-library R2 bucket, originals/ARD04.QF.003.pdf). Solid 4-sided rectangle boxes for free text (ACR-style, detected via mean-darkness horizontal/vertical scans at threshold ~100-120) and 3-group DD-MMM-YYYY comb boxes for every date field (DOB, Date of Latest Admission, Valid Authorized Stay, Date of Intended Departure), each measured individually via column-divider pixel scans and cross-checked with pixel-ruled visual crops. The Special Security Registration Number (SSRN) field is a single 22-cell comb box in a separate rounded-corner card shared with the staff-only Derogatory Record section.",
  "measurementNotes": {
    "columnAssignmentCorrections": "Two real column-order errors were caught and corrected before building this config, both by direct pdftotext -bbox xMin inspection rather than assuming left-to-right reading order equals left-to-right page position: (1) 'Passport Number' is actually the LEFT column field (xMin 18.19pt) and 'Date of Latest Admission' is actually the RIGHT column field (xMin 319.35pt) on the same row -- the opposite of the naive reading-order assumption; (2) on the 'Date of Intended Departure / Next City/Country of Destination' row, the Date of Intended Departure comb occupies only the narrow left portion of the row (pt 17.52-169.56) and the Next City/Country of Destination free-text box fills essentially the entire remaining width (pt 186.0-592.8) -- not a 50/50 left-right split as a first pass assumed.",
    "ssrnCellCount": "The SSRN comb box was measured directly via column-divider pixel detection and a pixel-ruled visual overlay crop (not assumed): 23 divider points, confirming 22 cells, not a round number like 20. Bound as a single flat dataKey (ssrn) written across all 22 cells, the same pattern already used for ADM05.QF.001's 8-cell dateRequested comb, since the printed field has no internal DD-MMM-YYYY grouping.",
    "derogatoryRecordAndVerifierStaffOnly": "The 'Derogatory Record:' two blank lines and the 'Derogatory Verifier' / 'Date and Time (DD MMM YYYY/HH:MM)' signature-style line beneath them are explicitly BI-staff-only per the form's own layout (positioned inside the same card as the SSRN field, which only BI staff complete at intake/clearance). All four are mapped as suppliedBy:staff, visibleTo:staff only, optional (staffFieldRequirements required:false) -- never auto-filled with fabricated content, consistent with every other form's staff-only-field policy.",
    "fourDateCombsShareColumnGrids": "Date of Latest Admission and Valid Authorized Stay are vertically stacked in the same right-hand column and use the identical colsPt column-divider x-positions (measured once, confirmed present at both row y-positions via a direct pixel scan of each row independently, not assumed from the first measurement alone).",
    "consentParagraphAndSignatureNotPopulated": "The Prosecution Clause and Data Privacy Consent paragraph's two inline name blanks ('I, ___, personally or through my agent/representative ___') and the bottom-of-form Date / Applicant's Signature over Printed Name line are wet-ink declaration elements, deliberately left blank by this automation -- same policy as every other mapped form. Only the signatureBlock's dateLine and signatureLine coordinates are recorded (for a future wet-ink completion UI), never auto-filled.",
    "mobileNumberPrefixHandling": "The Mobile Number box has a static printed '+63' prefix inside the box itself (confirmed via pdftotext -bbox: the glyphs end at xMax 35.49pt). freeTextFields.mobileNumber's xStartPt begins at 40pt, after the printed prefix, so the applicant's own digits are never drawn on top of it; sample data supplies only the digits after the country code."
  },
