  "mediaBoxOriginNote": "This PDF (unlike every other mapped form) has a non-zero MediaBox lower-left y (MediaBox: 0.00 7.29 612.00 971.04, confirmed via `pdfinfo -box`), a Canva export artifact. pdf-lib draws text/boxes using the PDF's raw content-stream coordinates, which follow the real MediaBox, not a normalized (0,0)-origin page -- so every yTopPt/yBottomPt/baselinePt below is the TRUE content-space y (visual-bottom-of-page y=7.29, visual-top y=971.04), not a naive pageHeight-minus-topdown value assuming a zero origin. Caught by a first generated test PDF rendering every field's text systematically ~7-10pt too low, overlapping the row below -- root-caused by comparing the rendered text's actual pixel position against the expected baseline pixel position, which differed by almost exactly 7.29pt (the MediaBox offset), then confirmed directly via `pdfinfo -box`. pageWidthPt needed no equivalent correction (MediaBox xMin is 0)."
